                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "60b2ee31-2cad-32e9-8a54-370e6011002f",
                        "entry_id": "aff724f2-5e1a-3c98-9b70-b4a212a7e12b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who is charged; the person on whom a charge is levied, who is charged with a crime, who is charged to do something, etc."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb005688-e307-4b6b-a103-e0a936f9f077",
                                "sense_id": "60b2ee31-2cad-32e9-8a54-370e6011002f",
                                "text": "June 18, charge to the Industrial Rehabilitiation Finance Board securing all sums which the chargees may be called upon to pay under or by reason of a guarantee;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "85bee783-516e-4cc8-9c42-dee776a50a88",
                                "sense_id": "60b2ee31-2cad-32e9-8a54-370e6011002f",
                                "text": "The most important point in the prehearing thinking was that both the charger and the chargee were African Americans."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ebf56a12-94ce-4d7a-831d-37aa72142858",
                                "sense_id": "60b2ee31-2cad-32e9-8a54-370e6011002f",
                                "text": "Imperative speech acts vary enormously in the relation of the speaker to the chargee, the purposes sought, the kind of situation, the presence or absence of a power of enforcement or threat of punishment, and many other features."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "696e0c4f-eb71-47cb-9a96-1eca27620520",
                                "sense_id": "60b2ee31-2cad-32e9-8a54-370e6011002f",
                                "text": "Charging modifies the first attack of the charger, and the first attack of the chargee."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f139327d-0e7b-36b8-a122-bf52c27c648f",
                        "entry_id": "aff724f2-5e1a-3c98-9b70-b4a212a7e12b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The holder or beneficiary of a charge or right in security (such as a debenture)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "671566f8-4bf8-4919-90c3-ccc494c99ce4",
                                "sense_id": "f139327d-0e7b-36b8-a122-bf52c27c648f",
                                "text": "A chargee proposing to sell or grant a lease of an object under paragraph 1 otherwise than pursuant to a court order shall give reasonable prior notice in writing of the proposed sale or lease to interested persons."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b071076c-d138-4162-bf95-5bb012be4522",
                                "sense_id": "f139327d-0e7b-36b8-a122-bf52c27c648f",
                                "text": "A charge differs from a trust because the chargee's right to the chargor's right is defeasible upon the chargor paying what he owes."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "97a77367-0dbd-3bb6-82b8-40bec21e2f96",
                        "entry_id": "aff724f2-5e1a-3c98-9b70-b4a212a7e12b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who is given charge of caring for another's animal or herd."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Africa"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8421208c-2f3d-4725-9082-6a866e3b965e",
                                "sense_id": "97a77367-0dbd-3bb6-82b8-40bec21e2f96",
                                "text": "But the chargee will be entitled to a proportionate abatement of the price of the animal if the carcass is later sold."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "70415c9b-e21f-42af-9f6b-98c16109012f",
                                "sense_id": "97a77367-0dbd-3bb6-82b8-40bec21e2f96",
                                "text": "Among the Yorubas, the first breed belongs to the owner of the animal, the next to the chargee, the third to the owner, and so on."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "692508c7-80d6-4b7e-b7d5-566be21bb235",
                                "sense_id": "97a77367-0dbd-3bb6-82b8-40bec21e2f96",
                                "text": "In the latter case the potential chargee made a direct approach to his relative, friend or neighbour who possessed livestock (goats, for instance) or was capable of procuring some, indicating his interest in being a chargee for his animal."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
